**The Job**

As Product Creation Process Manager, you own the seasonal Rolling Program and critical path across all STICHD brands, product categories and regions. You connect the internal teams involved in product creation, ensure clear milestones and accountability, and continuously improve the processes, systems and ways of working that take our products from concept to market.


You possess in-depth knowledge of operational processes, think cross-functionally, and proactively seek ways to improve and innovate the Rolling Program and the way we work.

**Your Mission**

* Set up seasonal Rolling Programs for all brands, product categories, and regions.

* Align cross-functionally between international teams and departments involved in the creation and execution of the Rolling Program.

* Monitor progress and ensure stakeholders deliver on their responsibilities to meet critical milestones.

* Continuously assess and improve the Rolling Program and related ways of working.

* Identify and implement improvements in processes, structures, and systems related to product design, development, marketing, and sourcing.

* Collaborate with departments such as Operations and Sales to support product creation and reduce lead time, cost, and effort.

* Support the department with additional relevant activities and projects as needed.

**Your Talent**

* You hold a Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Supply Chain, or a related field;

* Experience in process coordination, project management, or operations within a sports-lifestyle industry or international organization with global brands;

* Strong understanding of cross-functional workflows and critical path management;

* Excellent command of English, both written and spoken;

* Proficiency in MS Office (especially Excel and PowerPoint);

* Experience with project management tools is an advantage.

This role is based in Den Bosch, the Netherlands. Working remotely from other countries is not possible.




To apply for this role, you must already have the legal right to work in the Netherlands. We will not apply for work or residence permits.



